Firmware-specific properties for the imported Pad 4 / Find X9 Ultra data
======================================================================

oplus,pmic-pon-log-version (u32, /soc)
  Omit for the legacy phone PON event layout. Value 2 selects the Pad 4 /
  Find X9 Ultra layout. Their vendor sources assign VREG_READY_CHECK event
  0x20; infiniti, fairlady and both macan sources assign 0x15. The monitor
  translates legacy IDs before decoding; new IDs are not assumed on phones.

oplus,force-dwc31-revision (boolean, USB controller)
  Dengta alone selects the Find X9 Ultra vendor revision workaround. It
  forces revision 2.00a in suspend and 1.80a after host VBUS is disabled.
  Existing phone controllers omit the property and retain native behavior.
  This property requires the companion kernel DWC3 patch.

oplus,reg-otp-entry-size (u32, camera sensor)
  Lighthouse selects six cells per OTP record. Existing phones default to
  five cells. The sensor parser validates stride, record count and byte-sized
  fields before accepting a sequence; this property requires the companion
  camera module patch.

These properties describe source compatibility. They do not establish that
firmware, proprietary services or hardware work on a LineageOS image.
Dengta/lighthouse and Iceland must use their own firmware and calibration.
Dengta EVB3 is omitted because the supplied audio calibration is incomplete.
